{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.commuting_interfaces_brunnian_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.commuting_interfaces_brunnian_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L270-L282","doc":"**On the minimal interface set the only Brunnian carrier is trivial.**\n`σ₃` and `σ₆` are distant (`|3 - 6| ≥ 2`) hence commute, so `⟨σ₃, σ₆⟩` is free\nabelian and every word reduces to `σ₃^a σ₆^b`. Brunnian means every pairwise\nlinking number vanishes, which forces `a = b = 0`.\n\nSo no amount of extra word length produces a Brunnian carrier here — the\nobstruction is the generator set, not the length bound. The corpus's own\ncanonical `A = 3` carrier, the Borromean `(σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³`, needs **adjacent**\ngenerators and is therefore outside this subgroup entirely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.twoLk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.twoLk","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L257-L268","doc":"Pairwise linking numbers of a carrier `σ₃^a σ₆^b` in `B₉`, doubled to stay in\n`ℤ`: the `1|2` pair sees only the `σ₃` letters, the `2|3` pair only the `σ₆`\nletters, and the `1|3` pair sees neither.\n\n**The third component being `0` is an ENCODING of a reachability fact, not\nsomething proved here.** `σ₃` transposes positions `3,4` and `σ₆` transposes\n`6,7`, so no strand starting in block 1 (`1…3`) can ever occupy a position\nadjacent to a strand of block 3 (`7…9`): the two blocks never cross, at any word\nlength. Formalising that would need a braid-word model this file deliberately\ndoes not carry; it is stated in the header and taken as the definition of\n`twoLk`. Everything below is honest given that reading and vacuous without it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.carrier_underdetermined_by_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.carrier_underdetermined_by_binding","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L236-L253","doc":"**So the carrier is underdetermined by the binding itself.** In `B₉` there are\n**nine** band generators joining any given pair of nucleons (`3 × 3` strand\nchoices), and `countChannel` assigns all nine the same value. Combined with\n`QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition`, which makes the binding a sum over\ninter-component crossings, the binding-relevant content of a carrier is just the\nper-pair crossing counts — a triple `(m₁, m₂, m₃)`, not a braid word.\n\nMeasured, for a Brunnian carrier (`n₊ = n₋ = mᵢ` on each pair) with total\ncrossings `c ≤ 12`: **20 triples**, against **382,637,520** structured band\nwords — a collapse of about `1.9 × 10⁷`.\n\n**This is why a trace criterion cannot select the carrier, and it subsumes\nDefect 3.** The residual is being asked to make a distinction the binding does\nnot use. Defect 3 (the exact `1|2`-vs-`2|3` tie) is the two-generator shadow of\nthis: the trace ties them because the binding has no opinion either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.countChannel_depends_only_on_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.countChannel_depends_only_on_total","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L227-L234","doc":"**The count channel depends only on the total crossing count.** Two carriers\nwith the same `n₊ + n₋` on a pair give the *same* binding, whatever strands they\nactually use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.selfCrossing_not_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.selfCrossing_not_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L218-L223","doc":"Restated as the acceptance test it fails: a carrier is admissible only if its\ncount channel is non-zero somewhere, and a self-crossing carrier never is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.selfCrossing_countChannel_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.selfCrossing_countChannel_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L211-L216","doc":"**A carrier built only from intra-nucleon generators contributes no binding.**\nIt has no inter-component crossings, so both counts are zero and the channel\nvanishes identically — for every `q`, so no anchor or convention rescues it.\nThis is what the enumerator's rank-1 candidate `σ₈⁻²` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.countChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.countChannel","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L206-L209","doc":"The unsigned count channel, as in `BrunnianBindingChannel.countChannel`:\n`½(n₊ + n₋)(q − q⁻¹)`, whose `n₊`, `n₋` are **inter-component** crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.three_six_are_interfaces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.three_six_are_interfaces","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L200-L202","doc":"And `σ₃`, `σ₆` are. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.extended_generators_are_intra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.extended_generators_are_intra","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L192-L198","doc":"The four generators the enumerator's `..._extended` list adds beyond `σ₃`\nand `σ₆` are **not** interfaces, so the field name is wrong about two thirds of\nits entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.interface_iff_three_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.interface_iff_three_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L184-L190","doc":"**Interfaces are exactly the multiples of three.** So in `B₉` with three\nnucleons, `σ₃` and `σ₆` are the only inter-component generators, and\n`σ₄, σ₅, σ₇, σ₈` are all intra-nucleon self-crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.IsInterface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.IsInterface","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L180-L182","doc":"`σ_i` joins strands `i` and `i+1`; it is an **interface** generator when\nthose two strands lie in different nucleons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.blockOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.blockOf","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EnumeratorSelectionDegeneracy.lean#L175-L178","doc":"The nucleon block containing strand `s`, for nucleons of three strands each\nlaid out at `constituent_offsets = [0, 3, 6, …]`: strands `1,2,3` are nucleon 0,\nstrands `4,5,6` nucleon 1, and so on. ","signatureChunk":0}]}